  "shared_context_attribution": "MEASURED AND ATTRIBUTED. The affix-process co-create leg (categories._create_shared_process_context) created 13 shared members of PhPhonData.ContextsOS in this run -- 1 PhSimpleContextBdry, 7 PhSimpleContextNC, 5 PhSimpleContextSeg -- reported on 4 of the pair's 13 MoAffixProcess rules (26589ff1-2d00-437b-80d6-504422c28c65, 2ab66874-1548-4fb7-a5e7-172582ae7469, dd620446-a08a-4f69-a377-22fc937de511, de6df83e-3556-42f8-82fc-30d22d4a68b9). Every one is owned by PhPhonData in the source, which is the shared, project-level collection SC-010 is about. The count is the number of members CREATED, not the number of rules that use them: _resolve_process_graph consults member_targets first, so the second rule to reach a member finds what the first one made. THE BOUNDARY CONTEXT IS AMONG THEM, which is exactly what T107 could not say: 391e8cba-b951-4f1b-a64a-c5dc5fbe19c9, owned by PhPhonData in the source, was created by rule de6df83e-3556-42f8-82fc-30d22d4a68b9. So the destination's one PhPhonData-owned PhSimpleContextBdry came from the affix-process co-create leg and NOT from the phonological-rule path (Lib/categories._copy_context_cell), even though both write that collection -- the ambiguity T107 recorded is resolved by measurement rather than by argument. 5 rules reach that context through a rule-owned PhSequenceContext, reproducing T107's read-only count of five; the other 4 report no co-creation because they found it already present, and 1 of those never got that far (refused: 24ed706a-7df2-4609-a37b-2bfa28853ccc).",
